# English-only product copy (AuditIQ)

- All **user-visible text** in the AuditIQ app must be **English**: page titles, labels, buttons, table headers, empty states, aria-labels, `title` attributes, placeholder text, and mock/demo data shown in the UI.
- Keep **code identifiers** (TypeScript names, route parameter keys, API field names) consistent with the codebase; only translate what users see.
- Use **`lang="en"`** on the document root and locale **`en-US`** for Angular pipes (`LOCALE_ID`, `registerLocaleData` for English).
- Do not revert marketing names if they are proper nouns (e.g. **AuditIQ**, **DataVigil**) unless the user asks to rename them.

When adding features, default to English strings; do not mix French and English in the same screen.
